Installation

To install MacFile, just double click the MacFileInstaller application found in the archive you extracted and press the Install button. It will place all the files in their correct locations and show you a log of what it did. A link to the server portion of MacFile (afp_server) will be placed in your home/config/boot/launch folder so it will start automatically when you reboot Haiku (don't worry, this is a background process so you won't even notice it's there).

Prefer the terminal? Run ./install-macfile.sh install instead.

To Uninstall

Uninstallation is easy, just open MacFileInstaller again and press the Uninstall button (or run ./install-macfile.sh uninstall from Terminal).

What Next?

Once installed, open the MacFile preferences application to configure your file server for vintage Macintosh computers. Remember that this server only supports AFP2.2 and later, which means MacOS 8.0 throught MacOS X 10.5 clients. You can configure MacOS 7.6 clients to use the file server by copying the AppleShare Client from MacOS 8.x, but your results may vary, especially on devices with a 680x0 processor.

